<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaa3668b7429d3fc344953e947520184744bccbc4" commit="3a915d15c2eab7d24697f3d9c1c8c10f933238ce" commit_message="bluetooth: move property_handler_callback on ExportedObjectManagerWrapper  Class ExportedObjectManagerWrapper has property_handler_setup_callback_ private property that can only be set through method SetPropertyHandlerSetupCallback(). The property is only used when the method AddExportedInterface() is called.  This patch remove the property_handler_setup_callback_ property, and add a property_handler_setup_callback parameter to AddExportedInterface() instead.  This is needed to allow ExportedObjectManagerWrapper to be shared by many components so that those components can freely define the property handler callbacks per object/interface.  BUG=None TEST=Pass Test  Change-Id: Iaa3668b7429d3fc344953e947520184744bccbc4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1712840 Tested-by: Archie Pusaka &lt;apusaka@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Archie Pusaka &lt;apusaka@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Sasaka &lt;sonnysasaka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1712840" owner_email="apusaka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/40/1712840/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1ead265f314896728d30087b521e170e808b089b" commit="091591121474fd11ddd2698daf9947365d754c46" commit_message="camera.CCAUIModes: Temporarily disable the test  It interferes other tests and crash the tast bundle. Temporarily disable it while investigating.  BUG=b:138828180 TEST=None  Change-Id: I1ead265f314896728d30087b521e170e808b089b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1731418 Tested-by: Shik Chen &lt;shik@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Keiichi Watanabe &lt;keiichiw@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keiichi Watanabe &lt;keiichiw@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1731418" owner_email="shik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" ref="refs/changes/18/1731418/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idb49cb2a3a314307f65dec41d146a8293bba4fc2" commit="7961452224eea6671164066e11548d2c5e75861d" commit_message="cryptohome: Add new commandline features for cryptohome commandline tool.  To add new data restore key, simply type: cryptohome --action=add_data_restore_key --user=your_user_name Then type in your password, wait for a few second, then the hex string of data restore key will be displayed if authenticated.  To build authentication, testers can use switch &quot;--restore_key_in_hex&quot; to provide data restore key in HexString, for instance if testers type: cryptohome --action=check_key_ex --user=your_user_name --restore_key_in_hex=0123456789ABCDEF Cryptohome will use restore key in AuthorizationRequest and check if it can be authenticated.  To mass remove keys, users need to provide exempt key labels. Every other keyset whose label is not in exempt_key_labels will be removed. For instance, if users have four keysets which are labeled as &quot;l1&quot;, &quot;l2&quot;, &quot;l3&quot; and &quot;l4&quot;, say if they want to delete l1 and l2 and keep l3 and l4, they should type: cryptohome --action=mass_remove_keys --user=your_user_name --exempt_key_labels=l3,l4 After authenticated, l1 and l2 will be removed.  BUG=chromium:945057 TEST=Flash image to physical device and use cryptohome command line to test.  Change-Id: Idb49cb2a3a314307f65dec41d146a8293bba4fc2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-r